**WAKE: what the feedback says about the research, not just the site**
- **The "distinct" predictions are on a branch that is already excluded.** /mond-unification listed two predictions that differ from MOND: refraction of an external field, and gas density around a satellite at fixed external field. TEST-05 tested neither. Both belong to the density-keyed branch, which SPARC (+2843) and lunar laser ranging already rule out. So no galaxy-scale prediction that differs from MOND remains on a live branch. The proposal recommends the project lead adopt that as the galaxy-sector form of the "nothing distinct survives" sentence.
